				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/greenburger" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6546643); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6546643&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606616189" alt="Greenburger" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6546643)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/greenburger" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6546643); return false;" >Greenburger</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606615458 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">29 Nov 2020 02:04</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-50742/per-page-discussions">Per Page Discussions / Per page discussions</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/scp-5655/comments/show">SCP-5655</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4830779">
									

<p>This one has a lot of issues, but lets start with the positive. I like the idea of a decomposed justice-loving Santa. But your execution leaves a lot to be desired.</p>
<p>Firstly, there are a couple of plot holes. There are probably millions of crimes committed in the month of December in just America alone. If this SCP showed up for every single one, the foundation would have a serious problem preventing the public from finding out about it. To fix this, perhaps you can change the article so that this scp only appears for extremely heinous crimes.</p>
<p>The same goes for times when the scp shows up to give people presents. The scp showing up to give people presents could result in the public finding out about anomalies. The foundation needs a way to prevent the public from finding out, so either remove this bit or add a way for the scp foundation to track the scp so they can amnesticize individuals who were exposed.</p>
<p>The concepts also leaves a lot of unanswered questions. For instance, can the scp be in two places at once? If a bunch of people commit a crime at the same time but in different places, will the scp appear for only one person, or will a manifestation of the scp appear for all of the people.</p>
<p>Another question is if people have to &quot;fix their unlawful act&quot; for the scp to leave them alone, what counts as fixing an unlawful act. If you murdered someone, would you need to find a way to bring the person you murdered back to life. You need to create a specific set of rules that can be applied universally.</p>
<p>Additionally, you never specify what powers the scp has. Can it teleport? What if you try to fight it while the scp is trying to disembowel you. Does it have a way to immobilize targets through combat or an afflicted paralysis? That needs to be specified.</p>
<p>Finally, why do people exposed to the scp need to be killed if any unlawful act can summon the scp? That seems excessive and inefficient, which is why the foundation wouldn't do it. It seems more likely that the foundation would investigate what those individuals did. Additionally, why do the dishes/containers for the milk and cookies as well as the tree need to be incinerated. You said that was to prevent contamination, so is the scp diseased or something?</p>
<p>Lots of unanswered questions and glaring plot holes.</p>
<p>There are also lots of issues with you grammar scattered throughout the article. I'm not going to list them all since this is already a long post, but in the very first sentence you use is when you should use are.</p>
<p>You also have a bad habit of making you sentences to long by writing in a very indirect and convoluted way. For instance, you wrote:</p>
<p>&quot;SCP 5655 will manifest nearby an individual who has committed an unlawful act in the duration of the month December.&quot;</p>
<p>The first issue is that you tend to use a conjugation of &quot;is&quot; before every verb in this sentence (manifest and commit). You shouldn't do that sparingly at most. It would be better like this:</p>
<p>&quot;SCP 5655 manifests near individuals who commit unlawful acts in the duration of the month December.&quot;</p>
<p>Another way to cut down on fluff is at the very end of that sentence, where &quot;in the duration of the month of December&quot; can be shortened to &quot;during the month of December&quot;. That gives us a final edited version of that sentence:</p>
<p>&quot;SCP 5655 manifests near individuals who commit unlawful acts during the month December.&quot; Writing it like this is clearer and more concise. Most of you sentences have issues like this, which makes the overall article sound unprofessional, which takes away from the immersion.</p>

							</div>

								
					
