<p>An author getting the same feedback from two different people is often times a good thing! It means that the issue is deeper than a single reviewer's feedback, and it can be really helpful to hear that something isn't working for many people.</p>
<p>It's ok for two people to say the same thing, and they may even have unique ways of pointing out the same flaw that allow the author to glean more information and ideas!</p>

